+Joy Image Edit uses the joint-copy path for eligible CUDA FP16/BF16 image
+tensors of at least 32 MiB. It preserves image-first token order, copies
+values without arithmetic, and verifies each new shape/stride signature
+against the native concatenations before enabling it. Small inputs,
+unsupported layouts, gradient-bearing inputs, and unverified signatures
+during graph capture use the native path. This does not enable model-level
+BCG support.
